    "md5": "b0b4d196733bab2170930198ad2d42c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1573,
    "chunk_text": "Another heartwarming feature of this year\u2019s Paw-Sperity\u00a0 Xtravaganza will be the presence of children from the Indira Cancer Trust who will be treated to games and handicrafts at the Kiddies Play Area. It is hoped that as many children who are in the recovery stages will be present to enjoy some Avurudu cheer and Easter joy.\n\nRAS Co-founder Anusha David said she was delighted about the fact that 95% of the stall holders were those who had taken part in RAS\u2019 first ever fundraiser the Santapaws Extravaganza which was held on 1 December 2024. \u201c All the hard work, effort, and\u00a0 late nights are worth it when you have people placing their faith and trust in you. Animals have and always been my passion .\n\nAny animal or reptile is worthy of help, and all humans need to understand that without animals this planet cannot continue to exist. As a matter of fact we are witnessing its destruction right now. It\u2019s happening before our very eyes and if we do not act immediately it will be too late; very frankly it is already too late. It is not the remedy\u00a0 that is called for, but prevention , and an understanding that a quick fix can never be the solution. The development of our hearts and minds is required; mere investment in bricks and mortar don\u2019t amount to development.\u201d\n\nThe proceeds from the bazaar will go towards supporting RAS\u2019 street animal welfare work as well as their shelter, and their ongoing court cases with regards to the elephants .\n\nDavid was fulsome in her praise of all their partners who have collaborated with them over the years."
