    "md5": "3175e5af5b5f2931968d58567e802bc6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1886,
    "chunk_text": "NTB partners NCE to strengthen support for Sri Lankan exporters\n\nFrom left: NTB Senior Manager Development Banking Dhanushka Priyadarshana, Vice President \u2013 Commercial Banking Naveen Anthonypillai, Executive Vice President \u2013 Commercial Banking Arosha Liyanaarachchi, NCE Secretary General/CEO Shiham Marikar and Chief Operating Officer Inoka Perera\n\nNations Trust Bank (NTB) partnered with the National Chamber of Exporters of Sri Lanka (NCE) to support Sri Lankan exporters and strengthen export-led economic growth across the country. Through this collaboration, both NTB and NCE will work together to enable exporters through networking opportunities, extensive knowledge sharing platforms, recognition initiatives, and practical business enablement programs.\n\nThe partnership reflects the bank\u2019s continued commitment to empowering Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector by elevating entrepreneurs to build resilience, access new market opportunities, embed sustainability and deploy tools to increase productivity and become market leaders through long-term planning. By combining NTB\u2019s financial expertise and digital banking solutions with NCE\u2019s industry platform, the initiative aims to equip exporters with the insights, tools, and capabilities needed to enhance competitiveness in global markets. NTB\u2019s Commercial Banking supports Sri Lankan entrepreneurs with customised financing, trade and digital solutions designed to help businesses to scale up and gain competitive advantage in international markets. The Bank enables exporters to strengthen operational efficiency, expand market access, and pursue long term growth through expert advisory services tailor made for each business. These solutions are closely aligned with Sri Lanka\u2019s national ambition of fostering a dynamic, export-driven economy and positioning the country as a competitive export hub in the region."
  },
